</span></span></span></p>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposed profiling evaluation metrics.</span> To rigorously assess the profiling accuracy, we define two complementary metrics for each phase or kernel <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(1)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Accuracy <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></span> (%):
<span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(1)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}\;=\;\Bigl(1-\frac{\bigl\lvert\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}-t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,\bigr\rvert}{\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}}\Bigr)\times 100," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">α</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">LM</mi></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">GT</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">GT</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">100</mn></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}\;=\;\Bigl(1-\frac{\bigl\lvert\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}-t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,\bigr\rvert}{\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}}\Bigr)\times 100,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>LM</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>GT</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the latency measured by <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">lm-Meter</span> and the ground-truth latency, respectively, in milliseconds. <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the proportion of the true execution time correctly captured by <span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">lm-Meter</span>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(2)</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scaled error rate <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></span> (<math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\mathrm{s}/\mathrm{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\mathrm{s}/\mathrm{ms}</annotation></semantics></math>):
<span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text"></span></p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(2)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}\;=\;\frac{10^{3}\,\Delta_{k}\,[\mu\mathrm{s}]}{\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,[\mathrm{ms}]}\hskip 9.24994pt(\mu\mathrm{s}\,\text{per ms})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ε</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⋆</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">10</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">k</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">GT</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ms</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.930em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext mathsize="0.900em">per ms</mtext></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}\;=\;\frac{10^{3}\,\Delta_{k}\,[\mu\mathrm{s}]}{\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,[\mathrm{ms}]}\hskip 9.24994pt(\mu\mathrm{s}\,\text{per ms}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{k}=\bigl\lvert\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}-t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,\bigr\rvert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>LM</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>GT</mi></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{k}=\bigl\lvert\,t_{k}^{\mathrm{LM}}-t_{k}^{\mathrm{GT}}\,\bigr\rvert</annotation></semantics></math>. By normalizing the absolute error by the ground-truth runtime (in milliseconds), <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> measures the number of microseconds of error incurred per millisecond of actual execution time. This unitless quantity is typically on the order of <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, offering an intuitive sense of relative error magnitude.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> provides a direct measure of ground-truth coverage as a percentage (higher is better), while <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{k}^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> quantifies the absolute timing error normalized by runtime (lower is better). Together, these metrics offer complementary relative and absolute perspectives on the fidelity of the profiler.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2. </span>Phase-Level Profiling Performance</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase-level latency ground-truth.</span> To evaluate the accuracy of phase-level profiling, we first establish a trusted baseline reference using AGI, which does not natively support phase-aware latency measurement for LLM inference.
To enable AGI-based tracing for on-device LLM inference, we extend the MLC runtime with instrumentation support via the Perfetto Tracing SDK. Specifically, we define and insert phase-level annotations using the <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">TRACE_EVENT()</span> macro <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>)</cite> to mark key inference phases, such as embedding, prefill, decoding, softmax, sampling, and probability transfer to CPU. All events are grouped under a unified tracing category (e.g., “llm”), which is statically registered during runtime initialization.
During profiling, the target mobile device is connected via USB to a host machine running AGI. Upon completion of inference tasks, AGI generates a binary <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.perfetto</span> trace file, which we post-process to extract timestamped phase events. In parallel, <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">lm-Meter</span> captures phase-level timing data in real time, enabling a direct comparison against the AGI measurements.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06126v1/Figures/profiling_evaluation_prefill.png" id="S4.F2.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/85;" width="234" height="85" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Single <em id="S4.F2.sf1.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prefill</em> step. (Total absolute error <math id="S4.F2.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0.2739\mathrm{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.2739</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0.2739\mathrm{ms}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F2.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.06126v1/Figures/profiling_evaluation_decode.png" id="S4.F2.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/84;" width="234" height="84" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F2.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="S4.F2.sf2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">Three consecutive <em id="S4.F2.sf2.5.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">decode</em> steps. (Total absolute error <math id="S4.F2.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0.1643\mathrm{ms}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0.1643</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ms</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0.1643\mathrm{ms}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2. </span>Phase-level latency comparison between our <span id="S4.F2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">lm-Meter</span> and AGI ground-truth on Google Pixel 8 Pro running a quantized <span id="S4.F2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">gemma-2-2b-it</span> model (4 bit weights, 16 bit activations). Insets zoom in on the sub-millisecond segments, including <em id="S4.F2.9" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Embedding</em>, <em id="S4.F2.10" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">CopyProbsToCPU</em>, and <em id="S4.F2.11" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Sampling</em>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4. </span>Phase-level profiling accuracy on Pixel 8 Pro.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:205.9pt;vertical-align:-101.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-204.2pt,121.8pt) scale(0.5,0.5) ;">
<p id="S4.T4.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="S4.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:753.3pt;height:449.6pt;vertical-align:-222.3pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="S4.T4.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">

<span id="S4.T4.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
